WEBVTT

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:14.635
Rip Van Winkle and the Legend of Sleepy Hollow by Washington Irving.

00:00:14.695 --> 00:00:23.513
Copyright Black Cat Publishing.

00:00:23.573 --> 00:00:31.782
About the author.

00:00:31.842 --> 00:00:33.082
Name.

00:00:33.142 --> 00:00:36.305
Washington Irving, the father of American literature.

00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:37.075
Born.

00:00:37.135 --> 00:00:38.376
In New York City.

00:00:38.436 --> 00:00:39.297
When?

00:00:39.357 --> 00:00:41.929
April 3rd, 1783.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:43.190
First book.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.612
Knickerbacher's history of New York, 1809.

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:48.314
Most famous stories.

00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:53.018
Rip Van Winkle and The Legend of Sleepy Hollow, 1819.

00:00:53.078 --> 00:00:54.108
Travels.

00:00:54.168 --> 00:00:57.952
England, Italy, Spain, France.

00:00:58.012 --> 00:00:59.015
Died.

00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:10.993
1859 Rip Van Winkle Chapter 1 The Van Winkle family.

00:01:11.053 --> 00:01:16.524
The Catskill Mountains are west of the Hudson River in the British colony of New York.

00:01:16.584 --> 00:01:20.925
The colors of these beautiful mountains change with the seasons.

00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:24.576
There are many legends and stories about them.

00:01:24.636 --> 00:01:27.587
The year is 1765.

00:01:27.647 --> 00:01:31.768
Rip Van Winkle lives in a village at the foot of the Catskill Mountains.

00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:34.080
The village is of Dutch origin.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.573
Rip lives an old, ugly house.

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:40.064
He is a simple, kind man.

00:01:40.124 --> 00:01:44.386
Everyone in the village loves him because he is friendly and helpful.

00:01:44.446 --> 00:01:47.647
He plays with the children and makes things for them.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.528
Rip's wife is very harsh with him.

00:01:50.588 --> 00:01:52.699
She nags him all the time.

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:55.830
However, he is patient and obedient.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.821
He never gets angry at his wife.

00:01:57.881 --> 00:02:00.382
He simply keeps away from her.

00:02:00.441 --> 00:02:03.613
Rip has only one bad point.

00:02:03.672 --> 00:02:06.134
He doesn't like working.

00:02:06.194 --> 00:02:08.625
He only does the things he likes.

00:02:08.685 --> 00:02:12.177
He sits on a rock and fishes all day.

00:02:12.237 --> 00:02:15.318
He walks in the forest and hunts animals.

00:02:15.378 --> 00:02:17.600
He builds fences for his friends.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.571
He helps the women in their homes and gardens.

00:02:20.631 --> 00:02:24.221
He does everyone's work, but not his own.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.299
His farm is the worst in the village.

00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:30.920
He never looks after his land, his garden, or his house.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.891
His fences are broken.

00:02:32.951 --> 00:02:35.802
His cow eats the vegetables in his garden.

00:02:35.862 --> 00:02:39.223
His children's clothes are old and dirty.

00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:42.604
Mrs. Van Winkle nags him about his laziness.

00:02:42.664 --> 00:02:44.944
Poor Rip never says anything.

00:02:45.004 --> 00:02:47.756
He has a dog called Wolf.

00:02:47.816 --> 00:02:52.117
Mrs. Van Winkle doesn't like Wolf, and Wolf doesn't like her.

00:02:52.177 --> 00:02:55.453
She often throws things at the poor animal.

00:02:55.512 --> 00:02:58.600
Rip often goes to the village inn.

00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:02.954
It is called King George III in honor of the British King.

00:03:03.014 --> 00:03:06.878
There is a picture of King George outside the inn.

00:03:06.938 --> 00:03:10.612
The men of the village sit outside the inn during the summer.

00:03:10.671 --> 00:03:12.454
They talk and drink.

00:03:12.514 --> 00:03:16.308
They listen carefully to the schoolteacher, Derek Van Brummel.

00:03:16.368 --> 00:03:20.654
He is an educated man and uses long words.

00:03:20.714 --> 00:03:23.470
Nicholas Vetter is the innkeeper.

00:03:23.529 --> 00:03:26.872
He sits outside the inn from morning until night.

00:03:26.932 --> 00:03:29.884
Rip likes going to the inn and talking to his friends.

00:03:29.944 --> 00:03:31.266
He's happy there.

00:03:31.325 --> 00:03:35.008
But Mrs. Van Winkle doesn't like the inn or his friends.

00:03:35.068 --> 00:03:38.611
This is a place for lazy men, she says.

00:03:38.671 --> 00:03:43.204
You must never go there again, Rip.

00:03:43.264 --> 00:03:48.969
Page 16, exercise two.

00:03:49.029 --> 00:03:52.862
Listen to the following conversation twice.

00:03:52.922 --> 00:03:55.353
Then tick the correct answer.

00:03:55.413 --> 00:03:58.605
A, B, or C.

00:03:58.665 --> 00:04:00.817
Look at this house.

00:04:00.876 --> 00:04:02.828
All the fences are broken.

00:04:02.888 --> 00:04:04.208
You are right.

00:04:04.268 --> 00:04:06.410
You always build fences for Derek.

00:04:06.469 --> 00:04:08.151
He is my best friend.

00:04:08.211 --> 00:04:10.122
And I am your wife.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.683
I can build the fences on Tuesday.

00:04:12.743 --> 00:04:16.015
No, you must build the fences on Monday.

00:04:16.075 --> 00:04:19.195
But I must help my friend Nicholas on Monday.

00:04:19.255 --> 00:04:20.614
I don't like Nicholas.

00:04:20.674 --> 00:04:21.845
He's lazy.

00:04:21.905 --> 00:04:22.796
All right.

00:04:22.856 --> 00:04:25.078
I can build the fences on Monday.

00:04:25.138 --> 00:04:28.251
Then on Wednesday you must work in the garden.

00:04:28.311 --> 00:04:29.602
Yes, of course.

00:04:29.662 --> 00:04:32.294
On Thursday you must go to the market.

00:04:32.354 --> 00:04:33.776
What time is the market?

00:04:33.836 --> 00:04:35.437
It's at 9.30 a.m.

00:04:35.497 --> 00:04:39.040
and don't be late.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:50.418
Chapter 2 A Strange Afternoon One autumn day, Rip goes up the Catskill Mountains.

00:04:50.478 --> 00:04:54.338
After walking for many hours, he feels tired.

00:04:54.398 --> 00:05:03.700
He sits on a green hill and looks at the majestic Hudson River, and as he is looking at the sky, he says, It's almost evening.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.050
I must go home.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.141
My wife always gets angry when I'm late.

00:05:08.201 --> 00:05:11.492
As he's going down the mountain, he hears a voice.

00:05:11.552 --> 00:05:13.042
Rip Van Winkle!

00:05:13.102 --> 00:05:14.643
Rip Van Winkle!

00:05:14.702 --> 00:05:17.164
He looks around, but he sees no one.

00:05:17.224 --> 00:05:19.245
He hears someone call.

00:05:19.305 --> 00:05:21.016
Rip then winkle.

00:05:21.076 --> 00:05:22.567
Rip then winkle.

00:05:22.627 --> 00:05:23.528
Again.

00:05:23.588 --> 00:05:26.529
Then he sees a very strange man.

00:05:26.589 --> 00:05:29.971
He is climbing up the hill with something on his back.

00:05:30.031 --> 00:05:32.712
Rip thinks, Who is this?

00:05:32.772 --> 00:05:34.573
No one ever comes here.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.494
Perhaps I can help him.

00:05:36.554 --> 00:05:40.356
Rip walks towards the man and is very surprised.

00:05:40.416 --> 00:05:43.417
He sees a short, square, old man.

00:05:43.477 --> 00:05:46.728
He has long, white hair and a beard.

00:05:46.788 --> 00:05:47.989
Rip thinks...

00:05:48.049 --> 00:05:49.409
How bizarre!

00:05:49.469 --> 00:05:51.740
He's wearing very old clothes.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.641
They are Dutch clothes of the 1600s.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:56.592
Who is this man?

00:05:56.652 --> 00:06:00.853
The old man is carrying a small barrel on his back.

00:06:00.913 --> 00:06:04.074
Rip helps the man and carries his barrel.

00:06:04.134 --> 00:06:06.602
Together they go up the valley.

00:06:06.662 --> 00:06:12.603
Rip can hear the thunder, but he can't see the storm.

00:06:12.663 --> 00:06:17.367
Rip follows the strange man.

00:06:17.427 --> 00:06:20.666
He thinks, where are we going and why?

00:06:20.726 --> 00:06:24.174
Suddenly, they walk into a small amphitheater.

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:27.326
It is made of big stones and trees.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.768
There are some strange men there.

00:06:29.828 --> 00:06:35.490
They are all wearing Dutch clothes of the 1600s, too, and they all have beards.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.031
There is a captain.

00:06:37.091 --> 00:06:39.032
He is wearing a captain's hat.

00:06:39.092 --> 00:06:43.194
He is a big, fat, round man.

00:06:43.254 --> 00:06:46.246
They are playing nine pins.

00:06:46.306 --> 00:06:48.897
The balls sound the same as thunder.

00:06:48.957 --> 00:06:50.723
No one is speaking.

00:06:50.783 --> 00:06:56.032
The mysterious silence and the cold eyes of the men scare Rip.

00:06:56.092 --> 00:07:00.194
The old man points to the barrel and to the other old men.

00:07:00.254 --> 00:07:02.016
These men want to drink.

00:07:02.076 --> 00:07:03.266
Rip thinks.

00:07:03.326 --> 00:07:06.749
He serves them and then they continue playing again.

00:07:06.809 --> 00:07:09.261
Rip drinks from the barrel too.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.924
It is very strong but Rip likes it.

00:07:12.984 --> 00:07:15.595
He drinks again and again.

00:07:15.615 --> 00:07:21.298
Soon he falls asleep.

00:07:21.358 --> 00:07:25.881
Chapter 3.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.512
The next morning.

00:07:28.572 --> 00:07:33.383
Rip wakes up the next morning and says, it's morning.

00:07:33.443 --> 00:07:39.145
Then he remembers the old man with the barrel, the game of nine pins and the strong drink.

00:07:39.205 --> 00:07:41.066
My wife will be furious.

00:07:41.126 --> 00:07:42.556
What can I tell her?

00:07:42.616 --> 00:07:46.288
He looks for his gun and finds an old gun in its place.

00:07:46.348 --> 00:07:49.548
He calls his dog, but the dog does not come.

00:07:49.608 --> 00:07:52.480
Those old men have my gun and my dog.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.892
I must find them.

00:07:53.952 --> 00:07:56.116
He gets up and tries to walk.

00:07:56.176 --> 00:07:57.657
It's difficult to walk.

00:07:57.717 --> 00:07:59.618
My poor legs.

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.210
He thinks.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:04.512
He cannot find the old men or his dog.

00:08:04.572 --> 00:08:07.344
He is very hungry and decides to go home.

00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:12.038
He starts going down the mountain and when he is near the village, he meets some people.

00:08:12.098 --> 00:08:13.888
How strange!

00:08:13.948 --> 00:08:17.701
I know everyone in the village, but I don't know these people.

00:08:17.761 --> 00:08:19.773
Their clothes are very different.

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.344
Thanks, Rip.

00:08:21.404 --> 00:08:24.496
The people look at him in his clothes.

00:08:24.556 --> 00:08:27.477
They are surprised and they touch their faces.

00:08:27.537 --> 00:08:29.499
Why are they touching their faces?

00:08:29.558 --> 00:08:30.679
Rip thinks.

00:08:30.739 --> 00:08:34.021
He touches his face and is surprised.

00:08:34.081 --> 00:08:37.843
He has a very long beard.

00:08:37.904 --> 00:08:47.900
When Rip arrives at the village, the children point at his gray beard and the dogs bark at him.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:52.572
The village looks different.

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.443
It is very big.

00:08:54.503 --> 00:08:58.124
There are new houses with new names on the doors.

00:08:58.184 --> 00:09:00.396
He sees new faces everywhere.

00:09:00.456 --> 00:09:02.527
Everything is changed.

00:09:02.587 --> 00:09:05.290
Poor Rip is very confused.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.074
How is this possible?

00:09:07.134 --> 00:09:08.695
This is my village.

00:09:08.754 --> 00:09:13.767
I can see the Catskill Mountains and the Hudson River, but everything is different.

00:09:13.827 --> 00:09:16.328
It must be the effect of the strong drink.

00:09:16.388 --> 00:09:17.618
Rip, thanks.

00:09:17.678 --> 00:09:20.460
He finds his house and goes in.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:25.953
It is abandoned, and all the windows are broken and there is no door.

00:09:26.013 --> 00:09:28.544
There is nothing in the house anymore.

00:09:28.604 --> 00:09:32.666
He calls for his wife and children, but they don't answer him.

00:09:32.726 --> 00:09:34.108
What is happening?

00:09:34.168 --> 00:09:35.569
Where is my family?

00:09:35.629 --> 00:09:36.650
He thinks.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:38.523
He goes to the inn.

00:09:38.583 --> 00:09:41.546
He sees a big hotel in its place.

00:09:41.606 --> 00:09:44.020
Rip reads the name on the door.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.182
The Union Hotel.

00:09:46.243 --> 00:09:48.345
Jonathan Doolittle.

00:09:48.405 --> 00:09:52.168
He sees a tall pole in front of the hotel.

00:09:52.228 --> 00:09:54.728
On the pole there is a flag.

00:09:54.788 --> 00:09:57.390
There are stars and stripes on it.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:02.184
He goes inside the inn and looks for the picture of King George.

00:10:02.244 --> 00:10:04.826
He finds it but it is different.

00:10:04.886 --> 00:10:11.570
King George is wearing a blue coat instead of a red one, and he is wearing a hat instead of a crown.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:18.488
Under the picture, Rips sees the words George Washington.

00:10:18.548 --> 00:10:22.214
Chapter 4.

00:10:22.274 --> 00:10:32.211
The Spirits of the Catskill Mountains There are some people standing near the door of the Union Hotel.

00:10:32.271 --> 00:10:34.632
But Rip does not know anyone.

00:10:34.692 --> 00:10:39.036
They are not quiet, slow and sleepy.

00:10:39.096 --> 00:10:42.068
They all seem noisy and fast.

00:10:42.128 --> 00:10:46.316
They talk quickly in loud voices.

00:10:46.376 --> 00:10:49.774
Where are my old friends?

00:10:49.834 --> 00:10:51.084
Rips thinks.

00:10:51.144 --> 00:10:54.918
Rips sees a thin man with many papers in his pockets.

00:10:54.978 --> 00:11:01.724
He is talking about political elections, liberty, the war of 76 and Congress.

00:11:01.784 --> 00:11:04.746
These new words confuse Rips.

00:11:04.806 --> 00:11:06.718
What is this man saying?

00:11:06.778 --> 00:11:08.340
What is Congress?

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.641
Is it a town?

00:11:09.701 --> 00:11:10.752
What war of 76?

00:11:10.812 --> 00:11:13.094
Rips thinks.

00:11:13.154 --> 00:11:19.698
Soon, everyone is looking at Rip's long beard and strange clothes.

00:11:19.758 --> 00:11:25.030
The Thin Man asks him, Are you a federal or a Democrat?

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:27.771
Rip does not understand these words.

00:11:27.831 --> 00:11:32.471
An old gentleman asks Rip, Why do you have a gun?

00:11:32.531 --> 00:11:34.352
Do you want to fight?

00:11:34.412 --> 00:11:35.803
Oh, no, no.

00:11:35.863 --> 00:11:36.824
Says Rip.

00:11:36.884 --> 00:11:40.826
I am a poor quiet man, and King George is my king.

00:11:40.886 --> 00:11:42.878
What King George?

00:11:42.938 --> 00:11:44.739
The people cry.

00:11:44.799 --> 00:11:46.900
This man is a spy.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.531
He's not an American.

00:11:48.591 --> 00:11:49.842
Who is he?

00:11:49.902 --> 00:11:51.483
Call the police.

00:11:51.543 --> 00:11:55.932
The old gentleman asks, why are you here?

00:11:55.992 --> 00:11:59.440
I'm looking for my friends, but I can't find them.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.740
Rip says.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.531
Who are your friends?

00:12:02.591 --> 00:12:04.162
asks the old gentleman.

00:12:04.222 --> 00:12:05.502
Nicholas Vetter.

00:12:05.562 --> 00:12:06.672
Says Rip.

00:12:06.732 --> 00:12:08.093
Nicholas Vetter.

00:12:08.153 --> 00:12:09.464
He's dead.

00:12:09.524 --> 00:12:11.194
And Brom Dutcher.

00:12:11.254 --> 00:12:13.165
And Derrick Brummel.

00:12:13.225 --> 00:12:16.826
Dutcher is dead, and Brummel is a congressman.

00:12:16.886 --> 00:12:18.767
Says the old gentleman.

00:12:18.827 --> 00:12:21.990
Rip is unhappy and confused.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:25.850
I am alone in a strange world and no one knows me.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.963
Does anyone know Rip Van Winkle?

00:12:28.023 --> 00:12:29.488
He cries?

00:12:29.548 --> 00:12:31.982
Oh, Rip Van Winkle!

00:12:32.042 --> 00:12:33.384
Cry to people?

00:12:33.444 --> 00:12:34.284
Yes.

00:12:34.344 --> 00:12:36.106
He's sitting under that tree.

00:12:36.166 --> 00:12:40.038
Rip looks and sees a young man with dirty old clothes.

00:12:40.098 --> 00:12:41.320
Is that me?

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:42.991
Then who am I?

00:12:43.051 --> 00:12:44.192
Asks Rip.

00:12:44.252 --> 00:12:46.083
They look at him and say...

00:12:46.103 --> 00:12:48.685
He must be crazy.

00:12:48.745 --> 00:12:52.148
Then a young woman carefully looks at Rip.

00:12:52.208 --> 00:12:53.579
Rip asks...

00:12:53.639 --> 00:12:55.270
What is your name?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.212
Judith Gardner.

00:12:57.272 --> 00:12:59.580
What is your father's name?

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.738
Rip Van Winkle.

00:13:01.798 --> 00:13:07.064
Twenty years ago he went away and he never returned, she says.

00:13:07.124 --> 00:13:08.566
Where is your mother?

00:13:08.627 --> 00:13:10.098
Rip asks.

00:13:10.158 --> 00:13:12.451
She is dead.

00:13:12.511 --> 00:13:17.196
Rip embraces his daughter and says, I'm your father.

00:13:17.256 --> 00:13:18.898
I'm Rip Van Winkle.

00:13:18.959 --> 00:13:20.540
I'm old now.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:25.634
He turns to the crowd and says, Does anyone remember Rip Van Winkle?

00:13:25.694 --> 00:13:28.885
A very old woman says, Yes!

00:13:28.945 --> 00:13:33.447
This man is Rip Van Winkle senior, I remember him.

00:13:33.507 --> 00:13:37.058
Rip tells his incredible story.

00:13:37.118 --> 00:13:41.290
The people of the village can't believe his story is true.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:44.331
They ask old Peter Vanderdonk.

00:13:44.391 --> 00:13:47.542
He is the oldest man in the village.

00:13:47.602 --> 00:13:52.254
He knows all the legends and stories of the Catskill Mountains.

00:13:52.314 --> 00:13:58.353
Peter Vanderdonk says, Mysterious things happen in the Catskill Mountains.

00:13:58.413 --> 00:14:00.774
There are strange spirits living there.

00:14:00.834 --> 00:14:09.146
People say that every 20 years Henry Hudson returns to see his river and that he and his men play nine pins in those mountains.

00:14:09.206 --> 00:14:13.146
It is late, and the people of the village go home.

00:14:13.206 --> 00:14:19.522
Rip goes to live with his daughter and her family, and his son visits him every day.

00:14:19.582 --> 00:14:22.074
He is very similar to his father.

00:14:22.134 --> 00:14:25.578
He does everyone's work but not his own.

00:14:25.638 --> 00:14:27.920
Rip makes some new friends.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:29.521
Everyone likes him.

00:14:29.581 --> 00:14:36.968
He doesn't really understand the American Revolutionary War or the new nation called the United States of America.

00:14:37.028 --> 00:14:39.228
But he is a happy man now.

00:14:39.288 --> 00:14:44.290
He sits outside the Union Hotel and tells stories about the past.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:49.040
He also tells travelers about his 20-year-long sleep.

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:54.812
Some people believe him, but some don't.

00:14:54.872 --> 00:14:57.882
Page 35.

00:14:57.922 --> 00:15:12.598
Exercise 2 After his long sleep, Rip wants to know more about the United States, so he asks his friend, Congressman Derek Rummel.

00:15:12.658 --> 00:15:17.284
Listen to the interview between Rip and Congressman Rummel.

00:15:17.344 --> 00:15:20.425
Then tick the correct answer.

00:15:20.485 --> 00:15:23.344
Are we still a British colony?

00:15:23.404 --> 00:15:24.634
No, we're not.

00:15:24.694 --> 00:15:26.155
We're free now.

00:15:26.215 --> 00:15:29.026
So we're not a colony anymore?

00:15:29.086 --> 00:15:31.707
No, we are a new nation.

00:15:31.767 --> 00:15:34.558
What is the name of this new nation?

00:15:34.618 --> 00:15:37.489
The United States of America.

00:15:37.549 --> 00:15:39.552
Who is our king?

00:15:39.612 --> 00:15:41.314
There isn't a king.

00:15:41.374 --> 00:15:42.974
We're a democracy now.

00:15:43.034 --> 00:15:44.545
We have a president.

00:15:44.605 --> 00:15:45.976
A president?

00:15:46.036 --> 00:15:47.837
Yes, a president.

00:15:47.897 --> 00:15:50.438
The people of the United States choose him.

00:15:50.498 --> 00:15:54.300
In a democracy, everyone is free and equal.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:57.421
The people choose their own government representatives.

00:15:57.481 --> 00:15:58.392
Really?

00:15:58.452 --> 00:16:00.522
Can I choose the president too?

00:16:00.582 --> 00:16:01.943
Yes, of course.

00:16:02.003 --> 00:16:05.865
At elections, you can vote for the president of the United States.

00:16:05.925 --> 00:16:07.890
Who is the president now?

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:11.516
George Washington is our first president.

00:16:11.576 --> 00:16:17.369
George, but that's the same name as our king.

00:16:17.429 --> 00:16:21.250
Page 37.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.602
The American Revolution.

00:16:23.661 --> 00:16:25.492
Interview.

00:16:25.552 --> 00:16:31.645
A journalist from the Boston Gazette interviews general George Washington.

00:16:31.705 --> 00:16:37.114
Listen to the interview, then tick the correct answer.

00:16:37.174 --> 00:16:39.801
Hello, General Washington.

00:16:39.861 --> 00:16:41.752
What's happening in Boston?

00:16:41.812 --> 00:16:47.764
Well, there are 13 American colonies protesting against Great Britain, and I'm their leader.

00:16:47.824 --> 00:16:49.544
Why are you protesting?

00:16:49.604 --> 00:16:54.446
We don't want to obey British laws, and we don't want to pay taxes to King George.

00:16:54.506 --> 00:16:55.897
What do you want?

00:16:55.957 --> 00:16:59.378
We want to become an independent nation.

00:16:59.438 --> 00:17:01.392
What are you going to do?

00:17:01.452 --> 00:17:04.498
We are going to fight the British until we win.

00:17:04.558 --> 00:17:09.671
We have muskets, swords, horses, and many courageous men.

00:17:09.732 --> 00:17:12.203
We're called Yankees.

00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:14.884
But not all colonists are Yankees.

00:17:14.945 --> 00:17:18.036
Some are redcoats and fight with the British.

00:17:18.097 --> 00:17:20.738
What color are your uniforms?

00:17:20.798 --> 00:17:23.880
Our uniforms are blue and white.

00:17:23.941 --> 00:17:26.690
The British wear red jackets.

00:17:26.749 --> 00:17:32.659
On July 4th, my friends and I are going to sign the Declaration of Independence.

00:17:32.719 --> 00:17:34.130
What's that?

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:40.762
It's a very important document that says the 13 colonies are free and independent states.

00:17:40.822 --> 00:17:43.004
Good luck to you and your men.

00:17:43.064 --> 00:17:44.284
Thank you.

00:17:44.344 --> 00:17:49.616
Today, Americans still celebrate July 4th, or Independence Day.

00:17:49.676 --> 00:17:53.980
It is a national holiday.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:18:08.828
The Legend of Sleepy Hollow Chapter 1 The Headless Horseman Greensburg is a village on the Hudson River.

00:18:08.888 --> 00:18:14.470
Near this village, there is a silent valley called Sleepy Hollow.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.882
It is the quietest place in the world.

00:18:17.942 --> 00:18:21.786
The inhabitants are always a bit sleepy there.

00:18:21.846 --> 00:18:26.400
Some people say there are bizarre spirits in this valley.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:30.291
Others say there are strange voices in the air.

00:18:30.351 --> 00:18:36.043
The people of Greensburg believe there is a ghost in Sleepy Hollow.

00:18:36.103 --> 00:18:40.624
It is the ghost of a headless man on a big horse.

00:18:40.684 --> 00:18:47.126
Legend says, it is the ghost of a soldier of the American Revolutionary War.

00:18:47.186 --> 00:18:51.412
His body is buried in the cemetery near the church.

00:18:51.472 --> 00:18:56.078
Every night he rides his horse and looks for his head.

00:18:56.138 --> 00:19:01.880
He rides in the valley near the river, in the forest and on the roads.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:05.942
He always returns to the cemetery before daylight.

00:19:06.002 --> 00:19:12.795
Everyone calls him the headless horseman of Sleepy Hollow.

00:19:12.855 --> 00:19:23.839
Chapter 2 Ichabod Crane Ichabod Crane lives in Sleepy Hollow.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:28.774
He is a school teacher and comes from the state of Connecticut.

00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:31.696
He is tall and very thin.

00:19:31.756 --> 00:19:34.878
His legs and arms are very long.

00:19:34.938 --> 00:19:37.610
His feet are very big.

00:19:37.671 --> 00:19:43.576
His head is small with big ears, green eyes and a long nose.

00:19:43.636 --> 00:19:47.118
His clothes are always too big for him.

00:19:47.178 --> 00:19:51.494
Ichabod is always hungry and loves to eat.

00:19:51.554 --> 00:19:55.950
Ichabod is a good but strict teacher.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.702
His school is in the middle of the country.

00:19:58.762 --> 00:20:03.316
It has only one big room for all the pupils.

00:20:03.376 --> 00:20:09.770
After school, Ichabod plays ball with the older boys and on his free afternoons.

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:12.842
He walks home with some of the younger ones.

00:20:12.903 --> 00:20:19.245
He always chooses the boys with pretty sisters or generous mothers.

00:20:19.305 --> 00:20:25.736
Ichabod does not have much money, so every week he lives with a different family.

00:20:25.796 --> 00:20:30.298
He eats and sleeps at their house and keeps them company.

00:20:30.358 --> 00:20:37.322
When he changes family, he puts all his things in a big handkerchief and carries it with him.

00:20:37.382 --> 00:20:45.866
The farmers like him because he helps them with their work and the mothers like him because he plays with the small children.

00:20:45.926 --> 00:20:48.903
Ichabod also teaches singing.

00:20:48.963 --> 00:20:52.370
On Sundays, he is the director of the church choir.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:54.672
He is very proud of this.

00:20:54.732 --> 00:20:59.736
The schoolteacher is an important person among farmers and their families.

00:20:59.796 --> 00:21:06.731
Everyone respects him because he is educated and the women consider him a gentleman.

00:21:06.791 --> 00:21:10.944
Ichabod likes gossiping and being the center of attention.

00:21:11.004 --> 00:21:15.778
He also likes eating all the good food the women prepare for him.

00:21:15.838 --> 00:21:19.020
Ichabod loves reading books.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:24.224
One of his favorite books is History of New England Witchcraft.

00:21:24.284 --> 00:21:27.486
Ichabod believes the stories in this book.

00:21:27.546 --> 00:21:31.318
They are about ghosts and witches.

00:21:31.378 --> 00:21:35.902
During the winter, Ichabod often visits the old women.

00:21:35.962 --> 00:21:45.542
They tell him terrible stories about ghosts, haunted houses, haunted trees, and the headless horsemen.

00:21:45.602 --> 00:21:52.058
When he returns home at night, the sounds of the forest scare him.

00:21:52.118 --> 00:21:59.020
He thinks there are ghosts everywhere, so he sings church songs.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:04.531
A mighty fortress is our lord.

00:22:04.571 --> 00:22:12.347
Ichabod always sings these songs when he is afraid.

00:22:12.408 --> 00:22:18.354
Chapter 3.

00:22:18.414 --> 00:22:25.262
Katrina Ventassel Katrina Ventassel is one of Ichabod singing students.

00:22:25.322 --> 00:22:28.044
She is the daughter of a rich farmer.

00:22:28.104 --> 00:22:31.758
She is 18 years old and is very beautiful.

00:22:31.818 --> 00:22:35.483
She has rosy cheeks and a lovely smile.

00:22:35.543 --> 00:22:38.100
She always wears pretty clothes.

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:42.296
Katrina's father has a big home with beautiful furniture.

00:22:42.356 --> 00:22:47.618
He also has a fine farm, many animals and lots of good food.

00:22:47.678 --> 00:22:50.470
Ichabod likes her father's riches.

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:54.872
He also likes Katrina very much and wants to marry her.

00:22:54.932 --> 00:22:57.683
Oh, how I like Katrina.

00:22:57.743 --> 00:22:58.844
He thinks.

00:22:58.904 --> 00:23:01.264
How can I win her heart?

00:23:01.325 --> 00:23:04.096
Katrina has many admirers.

00:23:04.156 --> 00:23:06.932
They often visit the Vontassel house.

00:23:06.992 --> 00:23:08.938
Who does Katrina like?

00:23:08.998 --> 00:23:10.500
No one knows.

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:15.550
One day she is nice to one young man, and the next day she is nice to another.

00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:22.950
Brom Bones is the hero of Sleepy Hollow because he is tall, strong and handsome.

00:23:23.010 --> 00:23:25.331
He has broad shoulders.

00:23:25.391 --> 00:23:28.733
He is a bit rough, but always cheerful.

00:23:28.793 --> 00:23:32.956
He is an excellent horseback rider and a courageous fighter.

00:23:33.016 --> 00:23:38.488
Everyone likes Brom, but sometimes he is mischievous and plays tricks.

00:23:38.548 --> 00:23:41.086
He is Ichabod's big rival.

00:23:41.146 --> 00:23:49.696
Ram often visits the Fontassel House and courts Katrina, when his horse is outside the Fontassel House.

00:23:49.756 --> 00:23:52.999
Other admirers stay away.

00:23:53.059 --> 00:23:58.173
Ichabod also visits Katrina often because he is her singing teacher.

00:23:58.233 --> 00:24:06.910
He and Katrina sit together under the big tree singing and talking, or they walk together along the river in the evenings.

00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:11.068
Ichabod slowly wins Katrina's heart.

00:24:11.128 --> 00:24:16.708
Brahm is very angry because he wants to marry beautiful Katrina.

00:24:16.768 --> 00:24:19.220
He decides to fight Ichabod.

00:24:19.280 --> 00:24:21.440
But Ichabod doesn't want to.

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:23.412
Brahm is big and strong.

00:24:23.472 --> 00:24:25.523
I cannot fight him and win.

00:24:25.583 --> 00:24:27.204
Ichabod thinks.

00:24:27.264 --> 00:24:30.556
Brahm tries to make Ichabod angry.

00:24:30.616 --> 00:24:35.479
One night he goes into his school and he throws the tables and chairs about.

00:24:35.539 --> 00:24:42.862
The next day, Ichabod goes to school and says, Oh no, this is where the witches meet at night.

00:24:42.923 --> 00:24:48.718
Brahm is very mischievous and teaches his dog to make terrible noises.

00:24:48.778 --> 00:24:50.679
Then he tells Katrina.

00:24:50.739 --> 00:24:52.470
Listen to my dog.

00:24:52.530 --> 00:24:55.793
His singing teacher is Ichabod Crane.

00:24:55.853 --> 00:25:01.158
But nothing can make Ichabod fight, so Brahm is furious with him.

00:25:01.218 --> 00:25:02.969
I must find another way.

00:25:03.029 --> 00:25:06.574
Brahm thinks.

00:25:06.634 --> 00:25:12.790
